    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d196">

                <pb facs="0171" n="167" xml:id="pg167"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.30 Asiatic Fleet/481: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief, United States Asiatic
                        Fleet</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Yarnell</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chief of Naval
                        Operations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leahy</hi>)<anchor n="19" xml:id="d196-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-03T12:00:00+08:00">August 3,
                        1938—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>0003. Interview Chief of Staff Third Fleet, present my compliments Admiral
                    Oikawa, states [<hi rendition="#italic">state</hi>] that every effort has been
                    made to assist Japanese forces by sending <hi rendition="#italic">Monocacy</hi>
                    clear of recent fighting Kiukiang and informing them of all her movements.
                    Fighting is now over and though some mines may still be present it is obvious
                    duty demands United States gunboat promptly gain touch with American nationals
                    and assist them in every way; fuel also required. Request Admiral Oikawa issue
                    necessary instructions in order for <hi rendition="#italic">Monocacy</hi> to
                    proceed installation not later than Friday after [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >alter</hi>] your movements as necessary to keep in touch with <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ideumo</hi> until this matter settled. Advise
                    result.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d196-f1" n="19" type="source" xml:id="d196-f1-content">
                <p>Copy of telegram to the commanding officer of the U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Oahu;</hi> transmitted to the Department by the Navy
                    Department.</p>
